  "note": "Triennial election of the Warrenpoint Urban District Council (whole council, two wards), due 15 January 1932. There was no poll: East Ward had five nominations for five seats and in West Ward four of the eleven nominees withdrew, leaving seven for seven. Eleven nominations for seven seats; four withdrew (Peter McMahon, the outgoing chairman, Hugh Carr, Frank Fox and Thomas McGuigan), so the seven remaining were declared duly elected and there was no poll (Belfast News-Letter, 7 January 1932: 'There will be no contest in Warrenpoint'). Returned unopposed."
